# Commit and push after discrete work

When you complete a clear unit of work the user asked for (bugfix, feature slice, copy, config):

1. If you changed app code and have not already verified a successful build this session, run `npm run build`.
2. Create a commit with a short message focused on *why* (follow repo conventions; never commit secrets such as `.env`).
3. Push to `origin` on the current branch (usually `main`).

Skip commit/push if the user explicitly said not to commit, there is nothing left to push, or the task was questions-only.
